    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ac861a6d-2e0b-5829-b70f-24e6fe3ef861",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $E$ into the matrix $F$, where\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 16 & - \\frac{8}{3} & 8 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=\\left(-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 16 & - \\frac{8}{3} & 8 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=\\left(-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
