      ":question/id": "917fe128-cbd2-5be4-9152-cea56cdaa494",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix  $C$ into the matrix $D$, where \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -3 & - \\frac{15}{7} \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{4}{7}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -3 & - \\frac{15}{7} \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{4}{7}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$",
