      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $S$ into the matrix $T$, where\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 43\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{105}{2} & 0 & 105 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 43\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =\\begin{bmatrix}60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 43\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{105}{2} & 0 & 105 \\\\ 15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 43\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
